            <ArticleTitle>Menstrual cycle characteristics and risk of coronary heart disease and type 2 diabetes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2379-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.fertnstert.2010.03.044</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a prospective cohort study, we observed that women with a history of irregular cycles have a 28% increased coronary heart disease risk and tended to have a higher type 2 diabetes risk as compared with women who had a regular cycle length of 27 to 29 days. This association could not be explained by metabolic risk factors or altered hormone levels.</AbstractText>
